We shall leave r pointing at the offset of the first entry strictly greater than key.supplied PathStk is still valid.  See if it is for the correct key.Perform the normal BTree lookupPrivateBacks up the PathStk to refer to the previous entry in the tree. Returns TRUE normally, FALSE if there is no previous entry.this is a leaf pagehit beginning of current page: previous entry is left fatherthis is not a leaf page: previous entry is rightmost left sonObtains the OffsetTable associated with the BTree, if it is available; otherwise makes a new one.Gives back the OffsetTable.Bob Hagmann April 30, 1985 7:04:49 am PDTCatch File.Error and skip those pages during SalvageEntrieschanges to: SalvageEntries␀ù H␀␀ñ"Cedar" styleò␀headöúôIcodeöú
